   "evidence": "LightFront.lean:427-431; Physlib `Physlib/Relativity/LorentzGroup/Boosts/Basic.lean:57` defines `\u03b3 \u03b2 := 1 / Real.sqrt (1 - \u03b2^2)` and the file offers only `\u03b3_tanh`, `\u03b3_sq`, `\u03b3_zero`, `\u03b3_neg`, `\u03b3_det_not_zero` \u2014 no positivity lemma, so the proof must unfold the definition.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/LightFront.lean",
   "fix": "Factor out named lemmas (e.g. `LorentzGroup.\u03b3_pos (h\u03b2 : |\u03b2| < 1) : 0 < \u03b3 \u03b2`, and positivity of the two light-front boost factors) next to the boost lemmas, and use them here.",
   "issue": "`h\u03b3 : 0 < \u03b3 \u03b2` is proved inline by unfolding Physlib's definition (`simp only [\u03b3, one_div, inv_pos, Real.sqrt_pos]; nlinarith`), and the two boost factors `0 < \u03b3 \u03b2 * (1 - \u03b2)`, `0 < \u03b3 \u03b2 * (1 + \u03b2)` are likewise local `have`s. These are general facts about `\u03b3` and about `plusComponent_boost_two`/`minusComponent_boost_two`, hidden in a sign lemma and tied to \u03b3's current definitional form `1 / \u221a(1 - \u03b2\u00b2)`.",
   "line": 427
  },
  {
   "evidence": "LightFront.lean:411-412 against the declaration list at LightFront.lean:113-128 (no lemma expresses `p (Sum.inr 2)` via the light-front components); the same unfolding is redone ad hoc at LightFront.lean:294.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/LightFront.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public lemma beside `plusComponent_def`/`minusComponent_def`, e.g. `lemma apply_inr_two (p : Vector 3) : p (Sum.inr 2) = (plusComponent p - minusComponent p) / \u221a2`, and start this proof with a forward `rw` of it.",
   "issue": "`inr_two_pos_iff_plusComponent_pos` obtains `q (Sum.inr 2) = (p\u207a - p\u207b)/\u221a2` by a backwards rewrite chain through the `private` arithmetic helper (`rw [\u2190 add_div_sqrt_two_sub_sub_div_sqrt_two \u2026, \u2190 plusComponent_def, \u2190 minusComponent_def, \u2026]`). The `\u2190 *_def` steps only fire because the helper produced the exact syntactic form `(q (Sum.inl 0) \u00b1 q (Sum.inr 2)) / \u221a2`, so the step is fragile and the identity it establishes is invisible to other users.",
